			<div class="content" id="post-content-4450717">
									

<p>Boy, I hope I remember how to do this correctly.</p>
<p>This is my first attempt at uploading a skip in a long time. I'm trying to do something a little different from my past attempts that worked, but it's not too different. Please bring attention to any formatting errors&#8212;they're probably not deliberate!</p>
<p>I've included some of my thoughts about this piece in the collapsible, but my way of thinking about this is certainly not the only way&#8212;feel free to take it or leave it. Thank you for reading.</p>
<hr />
<p><strong>Image attribution</strong>:</p>
<p>This image is in the public domain and borrowed from the Internet Archive Book Images, page 629 of &quot;Florist's Review,&quot; 1912.</p>
<p><strong>URL</strong>: <a href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/internetarchivebookimages/16518073220/">https://www.flickr.com/photos/internetarchivebookimages/16518073220/</a></p>
<hr />
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Author&nbsp;opinions,&nbsp;interpretation,&nbsp;inspiration,&nbsp;etc.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hello!&nbsp;This&nbsp;is&nbsp;not&nbsp;the&nbsp;only&nbsp;way&nbsp;to&nbsp;read&nbsp;this&nbsp;skip!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I'll get this out of the way first: yep, in my head, this guy is portrayed by Danny Devito.</p>
<p>My political sympathies are probably clear enough. Still, I hope that I don't lean too hard in forcing an interpretation of Jimmy as truly benign or truly malign. I do think that the Foundation's tendency (in some canons) to cave to the irresistible temptation of using skips (often for very good reasons!) might be akin to opening Pandora's box. Someone's surely explored that in a more full and nuanced way than I did here, but it's a fun question to consider. I personally consider doubt and uncertainty to be a rich territory for dread, even when it grows out of a facially boring question like &quot;how are we going to run employee grievance proceedings?&quot;</p>
<p>I'm also very intrigued by the idea of a &quot;non-unitary&quot; Foundation&#8212;exploring the impact of competing factions, interests, and some of the divides that you see in every other part of society. I hope that some of this came through here in a way that you also consider intriguing and worth the read.</p>
<p>My vow: One day I'll write a skip that doesn't end with two collapsibles that contradict one another.</p>
<p>Inspiration, other than those mentioned in the skip, includes the bold and still-challenging <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-1851-ex">SCP-1851-EX</a>.</p>
</div>
