			<div class="content" id="post-content-4450966">
									

<blockquote>
<p>We secure, we contain, and we protect. And sometimes, those things protect us back.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is a fantastic line and I would adore this piece if there weren't some details that I feel are out of place. Namely, the incredible lengths the Foundation goes to try to kill Jimmy or lure him out. I get the commentary about the higher-ups seeing him as a threat, but the list of methods they've used to try to harm him is so extensive that it becomes comical.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>conceptual jamming, metaphorical dissolution, and other comparable physical and pataphysical assaults.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>A lot of this stuff is supposed to be esoteric as hell, and I can't see it being utilized for a threat that only appears 2% of the time. I also had concerns about the crosslinking to Series II, which is only justified by &quot;Jimmy likes these anomalies&quot;. Felt sort of OC-ish since there's not a greater narrative reason for their inclusion.</p>
<p>Otherwise this is right up my ally. I'd love an article about Foundation unions/managerial overstep/the Foundation's sordid past.</p>

