					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/erazm" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2819735); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2819735&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607200878" alt="Erazm" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2819735)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/erazm" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2819735); return false;" >Erazm</a></span> <span class="odate time_1576972917 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">22 Dec 2019 00:01</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4451573">
									

<p>Thank you, I appreciate the thoughtful critique. The points you take issue with include a few of my nagging doubts when I pulled the trigger on publishing.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Specific&nbsp;issues.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;seriously&nbsp;thanks&nbsp;for&nbsp;putting&nbsp;this&nbsp;so&nbsp;clearly!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I hoped that the redacted log would suggest a very large and serious intra-Foundation conflict, when the one right before that <em>wasn’t</em> redacted had to deal with XK-Class scenarios. Ultimately, it’s good to get feedback that an audience didn’t see it as suggesting something big or even something intriguing. The high and low-level addendums were also something that could have been handled with more care: I considered a whole fabricated story like “we need to quarantine any potential cognitohazards and keep this info among the low-level staff only” but was concerned it might have been a bit too much duplicity built into what is, at the end of the day, meant to be technical documentation. You’re also right about the strikethrough.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I’ll think over your comments and think about ways to edit and improve. Thanks again.</p>

