														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4452279">
									

<p>Theres a lot of dissonance in this skip for me, it feels like you're trying to be silly and serious at the same time.</p>
<p>-Jimmy ,no name, what a wacky guy huh?&quot;<br />
-Oh he has access to the entirety of the Foudation's history<br />
-Oh and his actions led directly to the <em>removal of an O5</em><br />
-But thats fine, the rest of the O5 aren't that concerned with this guy, and no one's doing anything to stop it because theyre lazy schlubs who now have less paperwork</p>
<p>I want to like it, and I was hovering over the upvote button, but its just&#8230;<br />
It doesn't feel like it follows a consistent internal logic, you really should have aimed lower than &quot;this guy unseated someone who's more powerful than POTUS and prevented the literal apocalypse from happening&quot; if you wanted it to be taken with a more light-hearted context of researchers being happy an anomaly is giving them less work to do, since the site directors will immediately fire the person that sent that letter at the bottom due to criminal negligence and refusal of work orders.</p>
<p>Concept is amazing, and super fun. Execution leaves me a little worried.</p>
<p>Downvote for now, but would really prefer to upvote all things considered, so fix it up a little</p>

